   ],
   "textLength": 3590,
   "text": "The other change that could make this a more viable option is significantly faster virtualization. Haiku B6 now has hardware-accelerated VMs, thanks to a port of the NVMM hypervisor. Although NVMM was originally written for NetBSD, it's not specific to that OS: first it was ported to Dragonfly BSD, and now Haiku thanks to a GSoC project. NVMM makes it possible to start QEMU VMs using the native vi",
   "counts": {
    "links": 15,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 6,
    "repeats": 6,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.06,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 1687,
    "height": 1449,
    "widthFraction": 0.83,
